                        "entry_id": "f0740880-e44f-3f7f-8faf-67b41c4f037f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who attends a banquet."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9751f07-176a-4f4a-839a-fb2587f9613e",
                                "sense_id": "a547bc15-1970-3de7-bd23-060a910df8ff",
                                "text": "The dinner and the soiree too were done,\nThe supper too discuss’d, the dames admired,\nThe banqueteers had dropp’d off one by one—\nThe song was silent, and the dance expired:"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5b43e8cd-d54a-44b6-bcb9-38cdf4dd2ea7",
                                "sense_id": "a547bc15-1970-3de7-bd23-060a910df8ff",
                                "text": "The banqueteers forsook their scented alcoves, and men of all stations withdrew from the outlying sectors […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f88a36b8-8c8e-447b-bf68-fdd541c9c56e",
                                "sense_id": "a547bc15-1970-3de7-bd23-060a910df8ff",
                                "text": "After a trumpet had given the starting sign each banqueteer tried to empty his jug as fast as possible, which must have been quite a feat, since a jug contained about three liters of wine!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
